-- title:
--   ̄ j(q^{Mℓ}) avoids the Igusa function field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and a natural number $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\kappa$, that is: a modular form `form` of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M) \le \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, together with a power series `series` over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose image under $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}$ is the $q$-expansion of `form` (with respect to width $1$), subject to the condition that the reduction `intSeriesC κ series`, the Laurent series over $\kappa$ obtained from `series` by coefficientwise reduction, is nonzero. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq p$ and $\ell \nmid M$. The assertion is that the element `jqNModC κ (M * ℓ)` of $\kappa((q))$ — namely the image of the reduced $j$-expansion $q^{-1}\,\overline{\mathrm{jNum}}(q)$ under the ring homomorphism `qExpand` substituting $q \mapsto q^{M\ell}$, so $\bar j(q^{M\ell})$ — does not lie in `igusaFunctionFieldX1C κ M w`, the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the union of `x1FunctionFieldC κ M` (the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $\kappa$) with the single element $(\mathtt{intSeriesC}\ \kappa\ w.\mathtt{series})^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the non-membership statement underlying the computation of the degree of the Igusa tower at level prime to $p$: the $q$-expansion $\bar j(q^{M\ell})$ generates a proper extension of the Igusa function field attached to $X_1(M)$ in characteristic $p$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq), which identifies the degree of the extension so generated.
